note Translation of tokio sync/oneshot.rs Sender::poll_closed

note GAP: poll-based futures - the original is a hand-written Future step: it is called repeatedly by an executor with a task Context, returns Ready or Pending, and registers a Waker so the executor knows when to call again; the doc's only concurrency forms are `together`, `pipeline` and `workflow`, which hide scheduling entirely, so the Poll result, the Context and the Waker are all declared here as opaque types
choice Poll
    Ready
    Pending

type TaskContext
type Waker

note GAP: atomic state shared between two tasks - inner.state is an AtomicUsize read and updated by both Sender and Receiver with Acquire/AcqRel ordering; the doc forbids values shared mutably between tasks and has no atomics or memory ordering, so `SharedState` is a capability whose operations stand for the atomic loads and read-modify-writes
type StateBits
    note a snapshot of the bit flags (VALUE_SENT, CLOSED, TX_TASK_SET, RX_TASK_SET) read from the atomic

define bits is closed
    given bits is a StateBits
define bits is tx_task_set
    given bits is a StateBits

type SharedState
    note opaque: an atomic word shared with the Receiver

to load_state from shared with acquire_ordering
    given shared is a SharedState
    produces a StateBits
    uses shared
    note GAP: memory ordering - the doc has no way to name Acquire, so `with acquire_ordering` is an invented label word that only records the intent

to unset_tx_task in shared
    given shared is a SharedState
    produces a StateBits
    uses shared

to set_tx_task in shared
    given shared is a SharedState
    produces a StateBits
    uses shared

note GAP: unsafe cell access - inner.tx_task is an UnsafeCell<MaybeUninit<Waker>> whose validity is guarded by the TX_TASK_SET bit, and every access is inside `unsafe`; the doc's only escape hatch is `trust` with a reason and owner, so each unsafe block becomes a `trust` line before an operation on an opaque TaskSlot
type TaskSlot

to will_wake slot with context
    given slot is a TaskSlot
    given context is a TaskContext
    produces a Bool
    uses slot

to drop_task in slot
    given slot is an editable TaskSlot
    uses slot

to set_task in slot from context
    given slot is an editable TaskSlot
    given context is a TaskContext
    uses slot

type Inner
    field state as a SharedState
    field tx_task as a TaskSlot

type Sender
    field inner as a maybe Inner
    note GAP: inner is an Option<Arc<Inner>>; Arc is reference-counted shared ownership with the Receiver, and the doc has no shared-ownership pointer, only owned values and editable borrows

type Budget
    note the coop budget guard returned by poll_proceed

to trace_leaf context
    given context is a TaskContext
    produces a Poll
    uses context

to poll_proceed context
    given context is a TaskContext
    produces a maybe Budget
    uses context
    note `nothing` stands for Pending: the task has used its budget and has been woken to yield

to made_progress budget
    given budget is a consumed Budget
    uses budget
    note GAP: RestoreOnPending - the Rust guard restores the budget when it is dropped unless made_progress was called; that is a destructor with behaviour, and the doc's `hold` only releases resources, it cannot run different code depending on whether a method was called first

to poll_closed sender with context
    given sender is an editable Sender
    given context is an editable TaskContext
    produces a Poll
    fails with SenderHasNoInner
    uses context
    note WORKAROUND: `self.inner.as_ref().unwrap()` panics if inner is None; Scribe has no panic, so the unwrap becomes a named failure the original does not declare
    note UNCLEAR: whether `uses` must also list inner's state and tx_task, which are reached through a field of the editable sender but are shared with another task

    note GAP: the `ready!` macro - returns Pending early from the enclosing function if the inner poll is Pending; the doc has no macros, so each use is spelled out as a `choose`
    choose trace_leaf context
        when Pending
            give back Pending
        when Ready
            note continue

    note Keep track of task budget
    var coop starts at nothing
    choose poll_proceed context
        when nothing
            give back Pending
        when some budget
            set coop to some budget
    note WORKAROUND: the budget guard must be consumed by made_progress on every Ready path and simply dropped on the Pending path; with a `consumed` linear Budget, the Pending path at the end would leak it, so the guard is held in a maybe var and the rule is only kept by the notes below
    note UNCLEAR: whether a linear value inside a `maybe` var is tracked; the doc shows linearity only for files and connections

    var inner_found starts at nothing
    choose inner of sender
        when nothing
            fail with SenderHasNoInner
        when some value
            set inner_found to some value
    note WORKAROUND: the doc's `choose` binds the payload only inside the arm, so to use `inner` for the rest of the body it is copied out into a var, which then needs a second `choose` at every use; below `inner` is written as if it were bound
    note GAP: binding a maybe payload for the rest of the block (an unwrap-or-fail); the doc has no `let x be try ...` form for maybe values

    var state starts at load_state from (state of inner) with acquire_ordering

    if state is closed
        made_progress coop
        give back Ready

    if state is tx_task_set
        trust "TX_TASK_SET is set, so tx_task holds an initialised waker that only this sender touches" owner tokio_maintainers
        let will_notify be will_wake (tx_task of inner) with context

        if not will_notify
            set state to unset_tx_task in (state of inner)

            if state is closed
                note Set the flag again so that the waker is released in drop
                let ignored be set_tx_task in (state of inner)
                note WORKAROUND: the Rust code discards the result of set_tx_task; the doc shows no statement form for calling an operation and ignoring its result
                made_progress coop
                give back Ready
            otherwise
                trust "TX_TASK_SET was just cleared by this sender, so no other side reads tx_task" owner tokio_maintainers
                drop_task in (tx_task of inner)

    if not (state is tx_task_set)
        note Attempt to set the task
        trust "TX_TASK_SET is clear, so this sender has exclusive access to tx_task" owner tokio_maintainers
        set_task in (tx_task of inner) from context

        note Update the state
        set state to set_tx_task in (state of inner)

        if state is closed
            made_progress coop
            give back Ready

    give back Pending

choice SenderFailure
    SenderHasNoInner
